  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-161534",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "To find the domain of $f$, we need the intersection of the domains of the individual components.\n\n- The domain of the $1$st component $\\operatorname{csc}⁡t$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ $t\\ne n\\pi ,$  where $n$ is an integer.\n\n- The domain of the $2$nd component  ${e}^{-{t}^{2}}$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\n- The domain of the $3$rd component $(t-1)^{3}$ is  $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )$\n\nTherefore, the domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)$ is \n\n$$\nt\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\\,t\\ne n\\pi ,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
